cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this specification or its test vectors, please cite it as below."
title: "The Accountability Axis (α) for Agent Actions: A Verifiable Form — Specification and Test Vectors"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-15
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/KarinLuni/accountability-axis
authors:
  - family-names: Lunina
    given-names: K.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5586-738X"
abstract: >-
  A specification, test vectors and a dependency-free reference verifier for the
  accountability classification (alpha) of agent actions: whether an agent can be
  the accountable subject of what an action creates. Defines the trust boundary a
  declaration must sit behind, the composition of alpha with the reversibility and
  consequence axis (kappa), chain establishment outside agent control at plan stage,
  the obligation record naming a human as party to the obligation rather than as
  approver, and a verification procedure with three results: PASS, FAIL, UNESTABLISHED.
  Written so that OWASP AISVS C9.2 could reference it as the procedure behind a
  requirement.
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - accountability
  - authorization
  - OWASP AISVS
  - agentic security
  - human oversight
  - conformance testing
